  "entry": "code/README.md",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A single-page dashboard for planning which of the 338 Arp galaxies to image each night at an iTelescope site (visibility window, moon risk, cost), writing ACP plan files for the scheduled targets, logging each session with a quality rating, and tracking survey completion and the re-image queue. Season-level batch ACP generation and moon-data refresh are separate Python-script stages of the project and are not part of this page. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
  "source": {
